---
title: 'What is Nx? Smart Monorepo Build System & CI'
description: 'Nx is a build system with smart caching and task orchestration for monorepos and polyrepos. Ship faster and keep CI fast as your codebase scales.'
sidebar:
  order: 1
  label: Introduction
filter: 'type:Features'
---

Nx is a build system for JavaScript and TypeScript, with plugins extending it to any language. It runs the scripts you already have, whether that's a single project or a monorepo with hundreds.

{% youtube src="https://youtu.be/pbAQErStl9o" title="What is Nx?" width="100%" /%}

## What you get on day one

`npx nx@latest init` writes an `nx.json` and adds the `nx` package. Your `package.json` scripts keep working, and you can run them through Nx immediately:

- **Local caching** - [Cached results](/docs/features/cache-task-results) mean you never rebuild the same code twice.
- **Task orchestration** - Nx runs tasks in the [right order](/docs/concepts/task-pipeline-configuration), parallelizing when possible.
- **A project graph** - Nx reads your imports and package dependencies to [map how projects connect](/docs/features/explore-graph).
- **Affected execution** - [`nx affected`](/docs/features/ci-features/affected) runs tasks only for the projects your change touches.

None of that requires plugins, generators, a `project.json`, or a restructured repository, and none of it is gated on how large your codebase is.

## Challenges of monorepos

Monorepos have many advantages and are especially useful for AI agents to have more context and tools to make cross-cutting changes. As teams and codebases grow, a few problems show up that the day-one setup doesn't cover on its own:

- **Slow builds and tests** - Hundreds or thousands of tasks compete for CI resources. Nx Cloud [shares one cache across machines](/docs/features/ci-features/remote-cache) and [distributes tasks](/docs/concepts/ci-concepts/parallelization-distribution).
- **Flaky CI** - Longer pipelines lead to random failures and inconsistent results between local and CI environments. Nx [re-runs flaky tasks](/docs/features/ci-features/flaky-tasks) and [self-heals CI failures](/docs/features/ci-features/self-healing-ci).
- **Architectural erosion** - Without clear boundaries, unwanted dependencies creep in and projects become tightly coupled. [Module boundary rules](/docs/features/enforce-module-boundaries) fail the lint task when one is crossed.

## Start small, grow as needed

Nx is modular. Start with the CLI and add capabilities as your needs grow.

| Component                                  | What it does                                                                                                    |
| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Nx Core**                                | Task runner with local caching, the project graph, and affected commands. Works with any tech stack.            |
| [**Nx Plugins**](/docs/plugin-registry)    | Optional technology-specific automation (generators, auto-configured projects and tasks, dependency detection). |
| [**Nx Cloud**](/docs/features/ci-features) | Remote caching, task distribution, and self-healing CI.                                                         |

